1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,360
Independent living is often lost in the space
between “everything is fine” and an emergency:

2
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:15,900
one missed check-in, one small household
problem, or one favor nobody clearly owns.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,520
STAY gives Sarah one calm place for that
middle ground.

4
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:25,900
Today shows one thing at a time, an ordinary
home check, and useful context.

5
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:34,740
Every weather, device, utility, maintenance, and travel signal
in this demo is clearly labeled as simulated.

6
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:40,660
Access preferences make the same experience
work voice-first or touch-first.

7
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:48,460
Sarah can choose captions, more response time, higher
contrast, reduced motion, and repeated key information.

8
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:50,740
These settings change presentation.

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,540
They never change her safety policy.

10
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,420
Privacy is scoped by role and moment.

11
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,080
Routine details stay private.

12
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:07,560
Access instructions and location can appear only inside an
authenticated, assigned incident when Sarah’s plan permits it.

13
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,440
Now Sarah misses her Morning Safety Window.

14
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:16,400
STAY makes one deterministic check, waits through
the grace period, and checks once more.

15
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,480
Bedrock does not choose what happens next.

16
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,480
Sarah’s saved plan does.

17
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:26,080
After the second missed check, her Circle
plan opens an incident.

18
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:29,280
STAY has not contacted emergency services.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,080
Sarah asks Tom, a nearby helper.

20
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:37,420
Only the minimum incident detail is shared,
and every action enters the timeline.

21
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:38,720
Tom accepts.

22
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:40,140
Tom is on the way.

23
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,940
He now owns the response,

24
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:44,480
and the Circle sees the same update.

25
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:51,320
STAY also handles ordinary Help Requests, household
playbooks, availability, and privacy-filtered House Memory.

26
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:55,460
The deterministic workflows keep working if
the language model is unavailable.

27
00:01:56,180 --> 00:02:02,500
For Alexa Plus, STAY exposes ten goal-level
tools through a standards-based MCP server with

28
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:07,400
accessible text, typed structured content,
provenance, and Alexa-style widgets.

29
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:14,800
On AWS, Cognito protects identity; DynamoDB
transactions and an outbox preserve state;

30
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:20,820
Scheduler and EventBridge coordinate checks; WebSockets
and minimal email deliver updates;

31
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:25,080
and Nova interprets only redacted,
non-critical intent.

32
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:32,420
STAY does not contact emergency services, diagnose a
condition, detect a fall, or replace Alexa

33
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:33,380
Emergency Assist.

34
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:38,900
STAY helps people stay at home, stay
connected, and stay in control.

